1
00:00:00,233 --> 00:00:02,533
A nuclear submarine cleans
its own air,

2
00:00:02,533 --> 00:00:05,700
and today's reactor cores
are rated for over a million

3
00:00:05,700 --> 00:00:07,933
miles — so why does it ever
come home?

4
00:00:08,633 --> 00:00:11,767
Unlike surface warships,
submarines are almost never

5
00:00:11,767 --> 00:00:14,600
resupplied at sea.
Everything the crew will eat

6
00:00:14,600 --> 00:00:16,300
is loaded before they leave.

7
00:00:16,933 --> 00:00:19,900
Crews and machines need time
ashore too:

8
00:00:19,900 --> 00:00:23,367
US ballistic-missile
submarines average 77 days

9
00:00:23,367 --> 00:00:26,333
at sea, then 35 in port for
maintenance,

10
00:00:26,333 --> 00:00:28,400
with two crews taking turns.

11
00:00:29,067 --> 00:00:31,500
Food, maintenance, the
people aboard and the

12
00:00:31,500 --> 00:00:33,133
mission — those set the
clock.
